IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpfta-types`
IMPORT `cpfta-part2-practices`

-- Tests for ss 3 to 5 and the Second Schedule.  Every expectation is read off the
-- text of the section or paragraph named beside it.  For each of the 27 paragraphs of
-- Part 1 of the Second Schedule there is at least one scenario that is a specified
-- practice and at least one that is not.

§ `Tests -- Part 2, ss 3 to 5 and the Second Schedule`

§§ `3. Application of Part`

--                                     supplier res, consumer res, offer made in SG, offer sent from SG, accepted in SG, acceptance sent from SG
`no connection with Singapore` MEANS `Application Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the supplier is resident` MEANS `Application Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the consumer is resident` MEANS `Application Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the offer is made in Singapore` MEANS `Application Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`the offer is sent from Singapore` MEANS `Application Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`the acceptance is made in Singapore` MEANS `Application Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`the acceptance is sent from Singapore` MEANS `Application Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `Part 2 applies` `no connection with Singapore`
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` `the supplier is resident`
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` `the consumer is resident`
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` `the offer is made in Singapore`
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` `the offer is sent from Singapore`
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` `the acceptance is made in Singapore`
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` `the acceptance is sent from Singapore`

§§ `4. Meaning of unfair practice`

-- Unfair Practice Facts: in relation to a consumer transaction, does or says or omits,
-- might be deceived or misled, false claim, takes advantage, knows (i), knows (ii),
-- Second Schedule practices.
`a deceptive statement` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY
`a statement no one could be misled by` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY
`a false claim` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY
`taking advantage of a consumer who cannot protect own interests` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, EMPTY
`taking advantage of a consumer who cannot understand the transaction` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, EMPTY
`taking advantage without knowing of any vulnerability` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY
`a specified practice under the Second Schedule` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, LIST `Paragraph 14` TRUE
`a specified practice not made out` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, LIST `Paragraph 14` FALSE
`a false claim outside any consumer transaction` MEANS `Unfair Practice Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY

#ASSERT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `a deceptive statement`
#ASSERT NOT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `a statement no one could be misled by`
#ASSERT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `a false claim`
#ASSERT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `taking advantage of a consumer who cannot protect own interests`
#ASSERT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `taking advantage of a consumer who cannot understand the transaction`
#ASSERT NOT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `taking advantage without knowing of any vulnerability`
#ASSERT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `a specified practice under the Second Schedule`
#ASSERT NOT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `a specified practice not made out`
#ASSERT NOT `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` `a false claim outside any consumer transaction`

§§ `5(3)(b). Acts of employees and agents`

--                                      employee, in course of employment, agent, on behalf, within authority
`an employee acting in the course of employment` MEANS `Attribution Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an employee on a frolic of the employee's own` MEANS `Attribution Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an agent within actual or apparent authority` MEANS `Attribution Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE,  TRUE
`an agent acting beyond authority` MEANS `Attribution Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE
`an agent not acting on behalf of the person` MEANS `Attribution Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the act or omission of an employee or agent is also that of the person` `an employee acting in the course of employment`
#ASSERT NOT `the act or omission of an employee or agent is also that of the person` `an employee on a frolic of the employee's own`
#ASSERT `the act or omission of an employee or agent is also that of the person` `an agent within actual or apparent authority`
#ASSERT NOT `the act or omission of an employee or agent is also that of the person` `an agent acting beyond authority`
#ASSERT NOT `the act or omission of an employee or agent is also that of the person` `an agent not acting on behalf of the person`

§§ `Second Schedule, Part 2 -- Interpretation`

-- Unsolicited Facts: supplied to a consumer in relation to a consumer transaction,
-- requested, only ground for the request is payment/use/similar/inaction, knows or
-- ought to have known meant for another, reasonable to believe unsolicited if
-- delivered to the other, continuing basis, material change, consented in writing,
-- only ground for consent is payment/use/similar/inaction.
`goods nobody asked for` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`goods the consumer asked for` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`goods said to be asked for only because the consumer paid or did nothing` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`goods the consumer knew were for someone else` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`goods the consumer knew were for someone else who would not have asked` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a continuing supply changed without consent` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a continuing supply changed with written consent` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a continuing supply changed with consent inferred only from inaction` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a continuing supply not changed` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a supply not made to a consumer in a consumer transaction` MEANS `Unsolicited Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `goods nobody asked for`
#ASSERT NOT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `goods the consumer asked for`
#ASSERT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `goods said to be asked for only because the consumer paid or did nothing`
#ASSERT NOT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `goods the consumer knew were for someone else`
#ASSERT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `goods the consumer knew were for someone else who would not have asked`
#ASSERT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `a continuing supply changed without consent`
#ASSERT NOT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `a continuing supply changed with written consent`
#ASSERT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `a continuing supply changed with consent inferred only from inaction`
#ASSERT NOT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `a continuing supply not changed`
#ASSERT NOT `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` `a supply not made to a consumer in a consumer transaction`

-- Applicable Agreement Facts: agreement for supply, no supply until paid, price by
-- instalments, number of instalments not counting a deposit, deposit paid.
`two instalments and no deposit` MEANS `Applicable Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 2, FALSE
`one instalment and no deposit` MEANS `Applicable Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1, FALSE
`one instalment and a deposit` MEANS `Applicable Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 1, TRUE
`no deposit and no instalments` MEANS `Applicable Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0, FALSE
`two instalments but supply before payment` MEANS `Applicable Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 2, FALSE
`two instalments but no express instalment term` MEANS `Applicable Agreement Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 2, FALSE

#ASSERT `the agreement is an applicable agreement` `two instalments and no deposit`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement is an applicable agreement` `one instalment and no deposit`
#ASSERT `the agreement is an applicable agreement` `one instalment and a deposit`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement is an applicable agreement` `no deposit and no instalments`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement is an applicable agreement` `two instalments but supply before payment`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement is an applicable agreement` `two instalments but no express instalment term`

§§ `Second Schedule, Part 1 -- Specific unfair practices, paragraph by paragraph`

`an untrue representation` MEANS Representation OF TRUE, FALSE
`a true representation` MEANS Representation OF TRUE, TRUE
`no representation made` MEANS Representation OF FALSE, FALSE

-- Paragraphs 1, 2, 4, 8, 9, 12, 18, 21 turn on a made and untrue representation.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 1` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 1` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 1` `no representation made`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 2` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 2` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 4` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 4` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 8` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 8` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 9` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 9` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 12` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 12` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 18` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 18` `a true representation`)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 21` `an untrue representation`)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 21` `a true representation`)

-- Paragraph 3: a false or misleading representation concerning the need for goods or services.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 3` `a true representation` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 3` `a true representation` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 3` `no representation made` TRUE)

-- Paragraph 5: goods "new or unused if they are not or if they have deteriorated or been altered ...".
--   made and accurate (the goods are new), not deteriorated: not a practice
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 5` `a true representation` FALSE)
--   made and accurate (new), but deteriorated or reconditioned: a practice
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 5` `a true representation` TRUE)
--   made and not new: a practice
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 5` `an untrue representation` FALSE)

-- Paragraph 6: only "if the supplier knows it is not so".
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 6` `an untrue representation` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 6` `an untrue representation` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 6` `a true representation` TRUE)

-- Paragraph 7: knows or can reasonably be expected to know, "unless the representation clearly states any limitation".
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 7` `an untrue representation` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 7` `an untrue representation` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 7` `an untrue representation` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 7` `a true representation` TRUE FALSE)

-- Paragraph 10: a price substantially higher than the estimate, unless expressly agreed in advance.
--                                                                                  estimate, higher, agreed in advance
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 10` TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 10` TRUE  TRUE  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 10` FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 10` TRUE  FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph 11: a representation about rights, remedies or obligations that is deceptive or misleading.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 11` `a true representation` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 11` `a true representation` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 11` `no representation made` TRUE)

-- Paragraph 13: terms that are harsh, oppressive or excessively one-sided so as to be unconscionable.
--                                                                                   includes, harsh, unconscionable
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 13` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 13` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 13` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 13` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 14: undue pressure or undue influence.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 14` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 14` FALSE)

-- Paragraph 15: another supplier will honour a voucher, when the supplier knows or ought to know it will not.
--                                                                                   represents, knows or ought to know
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 15` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 15` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 15` FALSE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 16: an objective-form representation primarily made to sell, unless it states that it is an advertisement.
--                                                                                   objective form, primarily to sell, states it is an advertisement
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 16` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 16` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 16` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 16` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- Paragraph 17: representing that a particular person has offered or agreed to acquire, if the person has not.
--                                                                                   represents, the person did
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 17` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 17` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 17` FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph 19: gifts, prizes or free items the supplier knows or ought to know will not be provided as offered.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 19` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 19` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 19` FALSE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 20: a discounted price "for a stated period" that the supplier knows will last substantially longer.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 20` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 20` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 20` FALSE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 22: bait and switch: an invitation or offer and, with the intention of promoting different goods, any one of (a) to (d).
--                                                                       invites/offers, intent, (a) refuses to show, (b) refuses order, (c) refuses to supply, (d) defective sample
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` TRUE TRUE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 22` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph 23: omitting, concealing in small print, or misleading as to a material fact, in connection with supply.
--                                                                       omits, small print, misleads, would affect the decision (material), in connection with supply
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 23` TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 23` FALSE TRUE  FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 23` FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 23` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 23` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 23` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 24: taking payment when the supplier knows or ought to know it cannot supply within the period specified
-- at or before acceptance, or, if none was specified, within a reasonable period.
--                                                                       accepts, period specified, cannot meet the specified period, cannot supply within a reasonable period
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 24` TRUE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 24` TRUE TRUE  FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 24` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 24` TRUE FALSE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 24` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 25: asserting a right to payment for unsolicited goods or services.
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 25` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 25` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 25` FALSE TRUE)

-- Paragraph 26: an invoice for unsolicited goods without the prominent "This is not a bill" text,
-- unless the consumer has expressly acknowledged in writing an intention to accept and pay.
--                                                                       sends invoice, unsolicited, prominent text, acknowledged in writing
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 26` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 26` TRUE TRUE TRUE  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 26` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 26` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 26` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Paragraph 27: refusing a copy of the written applicable agreement on request.
--                                                                       written, no copy given, requested, refuses
#ASSERT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 27` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 27` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 27` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 27` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` (`Paragraph 27` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
